<title>GERMANY: Chinese 97/98 soybean imports put at 3.0 mln T.</title>
<headline>Chinese 97/98 soybean imports put at 3.0 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>China may import some three million tonnes of soybeans in the Oct/Sept 1997/98 season compared with an estimated 2.1 million tonnes in 1996/97, the Oil World newsletter said.</p>
<p>It pegged China's 1997/98 soymeal imports at 6.2 million tonnes, up fom 3.4 million estimated for 1996/97.</p>
<p>Oil World said it had received reports severe drought in important growing regions had caused damage to soybeans, groundnut and grains crops in the second half of July.</p>
<p>Chinese oils and fats imports in 1997/98 could also rise to 5.1 million tonnes versus 4.1 million in the current season, led by soy oil, palm oil and rape oil.</p>
<p>Rape oil imports in 1997/98 may double from 1996/97 to reach 660,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
